DESCRIPTION >
    Cohorts: weekly acquisition cohorts broken down by first-touch AI
    source, all-time (no date-range param in the source). Tenant-scoped;
    prunes via (site_id, timestamp). Faithful 1:1 port of
    api/routes/cohorts.js:65-85 (queryName 'cohorts_ai'). Identity rule
    #19a: GROUP BY distinct_id in the inner subquery, canonical stitching
    key. Typed-column translation (SCOPE_v3.md §2.6): properties.site_id ->
    site_id, event -> event_type, properties.ai_source -> ai_source (typed,
    LowCardinality Nullable).
    §7 NULL-SKIP ANALYSIS: argMin(properties.ai_source, timestamp) has no
    COALESCE, but the query's own WHERE clause pre-filters
    `ai_source IS NOT NULL AND ai_source != ''` BEFORE the GROUP BY/argMin
    runs — every candidate row entering the aggregation already has a
    defined ai_source, so there is nothing left to skip. ai_source is
    genuinely Nullable in the typed schema (no DEFAULT per §2.6), so the
    same pre-filter applied to the typed column produces an identical
    candidate set to the live HogQL bag — no divergence, no fix needed.
    No JSON-bag fields.
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.

TOKEN "st_endpoint_read" READ

NODE cohorts_ai_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        formatDateTime(first_seen, '%Y-W%V') AS cohort_week,
        ai_source,
        COUNT(DISTINCT distinct_id) AS users
    FROM (
        SELECT
            distinct_id,
            MIN(timestamp) AS first_seen,
            argMin(ai_source, timestamp) AS ai_source
        FROM events
        WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
          AND event_type = '$pageview'
          AND ai_source IS NOT NULL
          AND ai_source != ''
        GROUP BY distinct_id
    )
    GROUP BY cohort_week, ai_source
    ORDER BY cohort_week ASC, users DESC
    LIMIT 1000

TYPE endpoint
